---
title: Keep Files After Reload
id: portable-snapshots-configure
order: 11
description: "Wire portable snapshots so a later run rebuilds completed sandbox files from your persistence."
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a sandbox chat. The agent writes files. The provider sandbox then goes\naway. The next run starts empty."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable snapshots save those files after each successful terminal run. A later\nrun restores the latest checkpoint into a new private sandbox. By the end of\nthis page, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" writes and restores those checkpoints."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one persistence value. Pass that exact value to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" and to\nthe snapshots object. Put "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page is enough for automatic save and restore. When you need a named\nversion, a fork, a download, or a file policy, add\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-save","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save a Named Version"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-fork","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Branch From a Version"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-artifacts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send a Frozen File"}]},{"type":"text","value":", or\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick Which Files to Keep"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-new-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create new persistence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memorySandboxSnapshots"},{"type":"text","value":" for local development. It creates persistence, a\ncheckpoint store, and the snapshot methods as one object. It does not load\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" at runtime."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  memorySandboxSnapshots,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst instances = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\nconst userId = 'user-123'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'app-builder',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst snapshots = await memorySandboxSnapshots({\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  context: { userId },\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, {\n      instances,\n      snapshots,\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can bind "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instances"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenant"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"locks"},{"type":"text","value":" at create time. A\nlater "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snapshots.save"},{"type":"text","value":" call can override those values. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-save","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save a Named Version"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instances"},{"type":"text","value":" in the same server module as this middleware. A named save\nmust use this same instance store."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the session "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"userId"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" for every run. Pass that same user id as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenant.userId"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snapshots.save"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reuse-existing-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reuse existing persistence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" already uses a persistence object, pass that same object\nto "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSandboxSnapshots"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not create a second message store."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The persistence object must include these stores:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"},{"type":"text","value":" (with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listForThread"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You also need a checkpoint store. That store is not a persistence store."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you already keep generated files, you already have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"},{"type":"text","value":".\nUse those same stores."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you only have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"},{"type":"text","value":" to that same adapter.\nSee "},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/build-your-own-adapter#which-stores-do-you-need","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which stores do you need?"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nand "},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/build-your-own-generation-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build a generation adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  createSandboxSnapshots,\n  InMemorySandboxCheckpointStore,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instances, persistence, sandbox } from './sandbox-server'\n\nconst snapshots = createSandboxSnapshots({\n  persistence,\n  checkpoints: new InMemorySandboxCheckpointStore(),\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, {\n      instances,\n      snapshots,\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"use-durable-stores-in-production","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use durable stores in production"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memorySandboxSnapshots"},{"type":"text","value":" is for local development and tests. Production needs\ndurable message, artifact, and blob stores, plus a durable checkpoint store."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The React chat example exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sqliteSandboxSnapshots()"},{"type":"text","value":" for a Node 22.5+\nserver. That function is an example adapter. It is not a package export."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use one SQLite transaction for every checkpoint write, head update, and blob\nreference count update. Use one transaction for a fork. The fork transaction\nmust also copy the source conversation. It must reject a destination thread\nthat already has persisted state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"writer-leases","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Writer leases"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each thread has one checkpoint writer lease."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A second run for the same thread gets a writer conflict while the lease is\nactive."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The middleware renews the lease while the run is active."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pause and detach paths release the lease. They do not publish a partial\ncheckpoint."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the writer loses the lease, the middleware does not publish the\ncheckpoint. A later successful run can create a new checkpoint."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-happens-on-the-next-run","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What happens on the next run"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A later run restores the latest checkpoint only into a new private sandbox. A\nlive resumed sandbox keeps its current files. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable Sandbox Snapshots"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for that restore rule."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instance durability finds a provider sandbox across server processes. When that\nsandbox is gone, portable snapshots rebuild the workspace. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./durability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instance Durability"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default policy excludes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".git"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env*"},{"type":"text","value":" paths. To keep\nonly some files, or one file, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick Which Files to Keep"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Read\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What a Snapshot Stores"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for secrets and restore\nsafety."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"create-new-persistence","text":"Create new persistence","level":2},{"id":"reuse-existing-persistence","text":"Reuse existing persistence","level":2},{"id":"use-durable-stores-in-production","text":"Use durable stores in production","level":2},{"id":"writer-leases","text":"Writer leases","level":2},{"id":"what-happens-on-the-next-run","text":"What happens on the next run","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a sandbox chat. The agent writes files. The provider sandbox then goes\naway. The next run starts empty.\n\nPortable snapshots save those files after each successful terminal run. A later\nrun restores the latest checkpoint into a new private sandbox. By the end of\nthis page, `chat()` writes and restores those checkpoints.\n\nCreate one persistence value. Pass that exact value to `withPersistence` and to\nthe snapshots object. Put `withPersistence` before `withSandbox`.\n\nThis page is enough for automatic save and restore. When you need a named\nversion, a fork, a download, or a file policy, add\n[Save a Named Version](./portable-snapshots-save),\n[Branch From a Version](./portable-snapshots-fork),\n[Send a Frozen File](./portable-snapshots-artifacts), or\n[Pick Which Files to Keep](./portable-snapshots-files).\n\n## Create new persistence\n\nUse `memorySandboxSnapshots` for local development. It creates persistence, a\ncheckpoint store, and the snapshot methods as one object. It does not load\n`@tanstack/ai-persistence` at runtime.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  memorySandboxSnapshots,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst instances = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\nconst userId = 'user-123'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'app-builder',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst snapshots = await memorySandboxSnapshots({\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  context: { userId },\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, {\n      instances,\n      snapshots,\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result\n```\n\nYou can bind `sandbox`, `instances`, `tenant`, and `locks` at create time. A\nlater `snapshots.save` call can override those values. See\n[Save a Named Version](./portable-snapshots-save).\n\nKeep `instances` in the same server module as this middleware. A named save\nmust use this same instance store.\n\nPass the session `userId` in `context` for every run. Pass that same user id as\n`tenant.userId` on `snapshots.save`.\n\n## Reuse existing persistence\n\nIf `withPersistence` already uses a persistence object, pass that same object\nto `createSandboxSnapshots`. Do not create a second message store.\n\nThe persistence object must include these stores:\n\n- `messages`\n- `artifacts` (with `listForThread`)\n- `blobs`\n\nYou also need a checkpoint store. That store is not a persistence store.\n\nIf you already keep generated files, you already have `artifacts` and `blobs`.\nUse those same stores.\n\nIf you only have `messages`, add `artifacts` and `blobs` to that same adapter.\nSee [Which stores do you need?](../persistence/build-your-own-adapter#which-stores-do-you-need)\nand [Build a generation adapter](../persistence/build-your-own-generation-adapter).\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  createSandboxSnapshots,\n  InMemorySandboxCheckpointStore,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instances, persistence, sandbox } from './sandbox-server'\n\nconst snapshots = createSandboxSnapshots({\n  persistence,\n  checkpoints: new InMemorySandboxCheckpointStore(),\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, {\n      instances,\n      snapshots,\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result\n```\n\n## Use durable stores in production\n\n`memorySandboxSnapshots` is for local development and tests. Production needs\ndurable message, artifact, and blob stores, plus a durable checkpoint store.\n\nThe React chat example exports `sqliteSandboxSnapshots()` for a Node 22.5+\nserver. That function is an example adapter. It is not a package export.\n\nUse one SQLite transaction for every checkpoint write, head update, and blob\nreference count update. Use one transaction for a fork. The fork transaction\nmust also copy the source conversation. It must reject a destination thread\nthat already has persisted state.\n\n## Writer leases\n\nEach thread has one checkpoint writer lease.\n\n- A second run for the same thread gets a writer conflict while the lease is\n  active.\n- The middleware renews the lease while the run is active.\n- Pause and detach paths release the lease. They do not publish a partial\n  checkpoint.\n- If the writer loses the lease, the middleware does not publish the\n  checkpoint. A later successful run can create a new checkpoint.\n\n## What happens on the next run\n\nA later run restores the latest checkpoint only into a new private sandbox. A\nlive resumed sandbox keeps its current files. See\n[Portable Sandbox Snapshots](./portable-snapshots) for that restore rule.\n\nInstance durability finds a provider sandbox across server processes. When that\nsandbox is gone, portable snapshots rebuild the workspace. See\n[Instance Durability](./durability).\n\nThe default policy excludes `.git`, `node_modules`, and `.env*` paths. To keep\nonly some files, or one file, see\n[Pick Which Files to Keep](./portable-snapshots-files). Read\n[What a Snapshot Stores](./portable-snapshots-safety) for secrets and restore\nsafety.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Keep Files After Reload\nid: portable-snapshots-configure\norder: 11\ndescription: \"Wire portable snapshots so a later run rebuilds completed sandbox files from your persistence.\"\n---\n\nYou have a sandbox chat. The agent writes files. The provider sandbox then goes\naway. The next run starts empty.\n\nPortable snapshots save those files after each successful terminal run. A later\nrun restores the latest checkpoint into a new private sandbox. By the end of\nthis page, `chat()` writes and restores those checkpoints.\n\nCreate one persistence value. Pass that exact value to `withPersistence` and to\nthe snapshots object. Put `withPersistence` before `withSandbox`.\n\nThis page is enough for automatic save and restore. When you need a named\nversion, a fork, a download, or a file policy, add\n[Save a Named Version](./portable-snapshots-save),\n[Branch From a Version](./portable-snapshots-fork),\n[Send a Frozen File](./portable-snapshots-artifacts), or\n[Pick Which Files to Keep](./portable-snapshots-files).\n\n## Create new persistence\n\nUse `memorySandboxSnapshots` for local development. It creates persistence, a\ncheckpoint store, and the snapshot methods as one object. It does not load\n`@tanstack/ai-persistence` at runtime.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  memorySandboxSnapshots,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst instances = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\nconst userId = 'user-123'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'app-builder',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst snapshots = await memorySandboxSnapshots({\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  context: { userId },\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, {\n      instances,\n      snapshots,\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result\n```\n\nYou can bind `sandbox`, `instances`, `tenant`, and `locks` at create time. A\nlater `snapshots.save` call can override those values. See\n[Save a Named Version](./portable-snapshots-save).\n\nKeep `instances` in the same server module as this middleware. A named save\nmust use this same instance store.\n\nPass the session `userId` in `context` for every run. Pass that same user id as\n`tenant.userId` on `snapshots.save`.\n\n## Reuse existing persistence\n\nIf `withPersistence` already uses a persistence object, pass that same object\nto `createSandboxSnapshots`. Do not create a second message store.\n\nThe persistence object must include these stores:\n\n- `messages`\n- `artifacts` (with `listForThread`)\n- `blobs`\n\nYou also need a checkpoint store. That store is not a persistence store.\n\nIf you already keep generated files, you already have `artifacts` and `blobs`.\nUse those same stores.\n\nIf you only have `messages`, add `artifacts` and `blobs` to that same adapter.\nSee [Which stores do you need?](../persistence/build-your-own-adapter#which-stores-do-you-need)\nand [Build a generation adapter](../persistence/build-your-own-generation-adapter).\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  createSandboxSnapshots,\n  InMemorySandboxCheckpointStore,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instances, persistence, sandbox } from './sandbox-server'\n\nconst snapshots = createSandboxSnapshots({\n  persistence,\n  checkpoints: new InMemorySandboxCheckpointStore(),\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, {\n      instances,\n      snapshots,\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result\n```\n\n## Use durable stores in production\n\n`memorySandboxSnapshots` is for local development and tests. Production needs\ndurable message, artifact, and blob stores, plus a durable checkpoint store.\n\nThe React chat example exports `sqliteSandboxSnapshots()` for a Node 22.5+\nserver. That function is an example adapter. It is not a package export.\n\nUse one SQLite transaction for every checkpoint write, head update, and blob\nreference count update. Use one transaction for a fork. The fork transaction\nmust also copy the source conversation. It must reject a destination thread\nthat already has persisted state.\n\n## Writer leases\n\nEach thread has one checkpoint writer lease.\n\n- A second run for the same thread gets a writer conflict while the lease is\n  active.\n- The middleware renews the lease while the run is active.\n- Pause and detach paths release the lease. They do not publish a partial\n  checkpoint.\n- If the writer loses the lease, the middleware does not publish the\n  checkpoint. A later successful run can create a new checkpoint.\n\n## What happens on the next run\n\nA later run restores the latest checkpoint only into a new private sandbox. A\nlive resumed sandbox keeps its current files. See\n[Portable Sandbox Snapshots](./portable-snapshots) for that restore rule.\n\nInstance durability finds a provider sandbox across server processes. When that\nsandbox is gone, portable snapshots rebuild the workspace. See\n[Instance Durability](./durability).\n\nThe default policy excludes `.git`, `node_modules`, and `.env*` paths. To keep\nonly some files, or one file, see\n[Pick Which Files to Keep](./portable-snapshots-files). Read\n[What a Snapshot Stores](./portable-snapshots-safety) for secrets and restore\nsafety.\n"}
